 "honest": [
  "the repo leg is not a discretionary allocation: it is the un-invested weight of the same engine, so 'cash drag' here means the accrual rate on dead weight",
  "x0 reproduces the historical zero-cash convention (cash=None -> 0.0 daily return)",
  "a multiplier is a counterfactual rate, not a rate that ever existed",
  "the per-book identity residual is rate x share minus measured attribution: the engine compounds on the equity curve instead of summing linearly, so a few bp of gap is expected and a gap above the published tolerance is a defect in the attribution, not a market fact",
  "descriptive census only: no gate, no verdict, no prereg, no trial count"
